\section{Threat Vectors on High-Value Astronomical Repositories}
Astrometric datasets (e.g., Gaia DR3 catalogs, high-resolution VLBI telemetry, deep-field FITS headers) require long-term confidentiality and data provenance. Conventional elliptic curve and RSA paradigms are inherently vulnerable to Shor's algorithm on cryptanalytically relevant quantum computers (CRQCs).

\section{Module-Lattice-Based Key Encapsulation (ML-KEM-1024)}
To guarantee quantum resistance across multi-decadal archival lifespans, we construct an ingestion pipeline utilizing ML-KEM-1024 (FIPS 203). The underlying mathematical hardness relies on the Module Learning With Errors (M-LWE) problem over the polynomial ring:
\begin{equation}
    \polyRing = \mathbb{Z}_q[X] / (X^{256} + 1), \quad q = 3329
\end{equation}

